      "defect": "EKS cluster has no admission policy controller deployed.\n",
      "infection": "The API server admits pods without policy evaluation. Image provenance controls (signature verification, CVE scanning, registry allowlisting) exist as individual checks but are not enforced at the admission boundary. Developers can deploy arbitrary images; policy compliance depends on team discipline and post-deploy scanning rather than pre-admission gating.\n",
      "failure": "No admission controller. Pod creation is ungated. Supply chain attacks succeed because there is no enforcement point between the developer and the cluster.\n",
